JAVA COLLECTION FRAMEWORK (COMPLETE STRUCTURE)

1. Iterable
- Type: Interface
- Extended by: Collection
- Methods:
  iterator()
  forEach()

--------------------------------------------------

2. Collection
- Type: Interface
- Extends: Iterable
- Implemented by: List, Set, Queue
- Methods:
  add(E e)
  remove(Object o)
  size()
  isEmpty()
  contains(Object o)
  clear()
  iterator()

--------------------------------------------------

3. List (Ordered, allows duplicates)
- Type: Interface
- Extends: Collection
- Implemented by: ArrayList, LinkedList, Vector, Stack
- Methods:
  add(E e)
  add(int index, E element)
  get(int index)
  set(int index, E element)
  remove(int index)
  indexOf(Object o)

   a) ArrayList
   - Type: Class
   - Implements: List
   - Methods:
     add(), get(), remove(), size()

   b) LinkedList
   - Type: Class
   - Implements: List, Deque
   - Methods:
     add(), addFirst(), addLast()
     removeFirst(), removeLast()
     get()

   c) Vector (Legacy)
   - Type: Class
   - Implements: List
   - Methods:
     add(), get(), size()

   d) Stack (Legacy)
   - Type: Class
   - Extends: Vector
   - Methods:
     push(), pop(), peek()

--------------------------------------------------

4. Set (No duplicates)
- Type: Interface
- Extends: Collection
- Implemented by: HashSet, LinkedHashSet, TreeSet
- Methods:
  add(E e)
  remove(Object o)
  contains(Object o)

   a) HashSet
   - Type: Class
   - Implements: Set
   - Methods:
     add(), remove(), contains()

   b) LinkedHashSet
   - Type: Class
   - Extends: HashSet
   - Methods:
     add(), remove()

   c) TreeSet
   - Type: Class
   - Implements: NavigableSet
   - Methods:
     add()
     first(), last()
     ceiling(), floor()

--------------------------------------------------

5. Queue
- Type: Interface
- Extends: Collection
- Implemented by: PriorityQueue, LinkedList
- Methods:
  offer(E e)
  poll()
  peek()

   a) Deque
   - Type: Interface
   - Extends: Queue
   - Implemented by: ArrayDeque, LinkedList
   - Methods:
     addFirst(), addLast()
     removeFirst(), removeLast()

   b) PriorityQueue
   - Type: Class
   - Implements: Queue
   - Methods:
     offer(), poll(), peek()

   c) ArrayDeque
   - Type: Class
   - Implements: Deque
   - Methods:
     addFirst(), addLast()
     pollFirst(), pollLast()

--------------------------------------------------

6. Map (Separate hierarchy - NOT part of Collection)
- Type: Interface
- Implemented by: HashMap, LinkedHashMap, TreeMap, Hashtable, ConcurrentHashMap
- Methods:
  put(K key, V value)
  get(Object key)
  remove(Object key)
  containsKey(Object key)
  containsValue(Object value)
  keySet()
  values()

   a) HashMap
   - Type: Class
   - Implements: Map
   - Methods:
     put(), get(), remove(), containsKey()

   b) LinkedHashMap
   - Type: Class
   - Extends: HashMap
   - Methods:
     put(), get()

   c) TreeMap
   - Type: Class
   - Implements: NavigableMap
   - Methods:
     put()
     firstKey(), lastKey()
     ceilingKey(), floorKey()

   d) Hashtable (Legacy)
   - Type: Class
   - Implements: Map
   - Methods:
     put(), get()

   e) ConcurrentHashMap
   - Type: Class
   - Implements: ConcurrentMap
   - Methods:
     put(), get(), putIfAbsent()

--------------------------------------------------

7. Utility Classes

a) Collections
- Type: Class
- Methods:
  sort(List)
  reverse(List)
  shuffle(List)
  synchronizedList(List)

b) Arrays
- Type: Class
- Methods:
  sort()
  binarySearch()

--------------------------------------------------

FINAL HIERARCHY (SHORT VIEW)

Iterable
 └── Collection
      ├── List → ArrayList, LinkedList, Vector → Stack
      ├── Set → HashSet → LinkedHashSet, TreeSet
      ├── Queue → PriorityQueue, Deque → ArrayDeque, LinkedList

Map (separate)
 ├── HashMap → LinkedHashMap
 ├── TreeMap
 ├── Hashtable
 └── ConcurrentHashMap